Per-session versus per-character (versus per-player, on systems without
real user accounts).

If I set DECgraphics or IBMgraphics, that's a per-session thing. Next time
I might be on a different terminal. If I play a lot on one terminal, I set
the appropriate option in my .nethackrc, and I expect that to affect all
saved games I load thereafter. It's not appropriate for this option to be
in the savefile.

That's (an example of) why there are volatile options.
